      "message": "The view never uses isError. So if loading the BMC manager fails, the page just shows a greyed-out \"Reboot BMC\" button and --, with no message telling the user anything went wrong.\n\nwhy: useManager() already calculates isError for exactly this case, but the view throws it away. The user can\u0027t tell the difference between \"still loading,\" \"something failed,\" and \"nothing to reboot.\" That\u0027s a confusing dead-end on a critical Operations page.\n\nrecommended changes: Also pull in isError and show an alert when it\u0027s true:\n\n```\nconst { lastRebootTime, reset, isLoading, isError, canReset } \u003d useManager();\n```\n\n```\n\u003calert v-if\u003d\"isError\" variant\u003d\"danger\"\u003e\n  {{ $t(\u0027pageRebootBmc.errorLoadingManager\u0027) }}\n\u003c/alert\u003e\n```",
